## 7. Constraints changed to use shadow values

I changed 4 constraints.

---

### A. `noUnderfillByBlock(...)`

### Before

It grouped block + seats and called `producedHoursForBlock(b, seats)` every time.

### After

It now works directly on `BlockDecision`:

```java
.filter(b -> b.producedHoursTotalShadow < b.requiredHours)
```

Penalty uses:

```java
int gap = b.requiredHours - b.producedHoursTotalShadow;
```

### Benefit

No more block-to-seat grouping for this constraint.

---

### B. `overfillAtMostOneDayByBlock(...)`

### Before

It grouped block + seats and recalculated:

* produced hours
* staffed count

### After

It now uses:

```java
int over = b.producedHoursTotalShadow - b.requiredHours;
return over > b.assignedSeatCountShadow * hours;
```

Penalty also uses the same shadow values.

### Benefit

No more repeated seat scan inside this constraint.

---

### C. `softBalanceBlockAvgSkill(...)`

### Before

It grouped seats by block and recalculated assigned count + skill sum.

### After

It now uses:

```java
.filter(b -> b.assignedEmployeeCountShadow > 0)
double avgAssigned = b.assignedSkillSumShadow / Math.max(1.0, b.assignedEmployeeCountShadow);
```

### Benefit

Average skill is now already available on the block.

---

### D. `recommendHeadcount(...)`

### Before

It grouped seats to count staffed seats.

### After

It now uses:

```java
int staffed = b.assignedSeatCountShadow;
```

### Benefit

Much cheaper and simpler.

